  "behavior": [
    "One closed cumulative host plan derives every scheduled frame/tensor envelope plus fixed claim/control and simultaneously retained receipt payload. Original-account H is protected before claim allocation; exact-scope child constructors never acquire another host hold. Claims, skips and failed/dropped construction are nonrefunding; only the same partial builder can resume.",
    "Completed tensor receipts bind private schedule custody identity, phase, prediction and selection. Same-shaped plans and banks cannot exchange receipts. Completed output aliases retain the whole original H. Native source pin rollback is limited to failed construction; subsequent failures preserve full exact-scope pins through linked quarantine.",
    "Additive core TextPreparationOptions reaches original admission before prompt/sampler work. Ordinary, controlled and detached starts use the existing runner and exactly one Instrumentation agreement, including explicit options with absent capture. The exact shared source retires after machine/failure payloads. Legacy starts and saved resume keep their previous ordering.",
    "Native retained inventory counts actual SharedCapturePlan nested capacities under a separate non-slot identity. Existing unquoted registration or exact funded scope attaches a once-per-domain charge, including earlier aliases. Partial attachment retains earlier charges; publication owns no cycle back to the shared source.",
    "Borrowed revalidation shares initial discovery-dependent checks and requires exact selected declaration equality. The original source supplies immutable geometry/origin/invocation invariants and the actual selection passed to estimation. Checkpoint validation avoids an extra whole-plan/digest reconstruction while retaining the distinct checkpoint-copy contract."
  ],
  "review_findings": [
    "Independent exact-source reviews covered the seven-file borrowed revalidation unit and eleven-file cumulative host unit. Root reviewed all options and source publication production/tests plus the cumulative host production and fixed worker reuse.",
    "First runtime compilation reported five E0505 errors caused by three test-only tuple drops moving owners alongside live borrowers. Sequentially dropping partial transfer, frame and then owners preserves the intended lifecycle. The failed log, exact three-hunk patch and independently reviewed corrected source hashes are retained. Production code did not require correction.",
    "Current native publication tests cover all eight transform payloads, actual spare capacities, aliases versus independent equal sources, multiple domains, coldness, exact/one-short credit, and partial poison/quarantine. Native tensor regressions reran after the private custody representation/fixed-worker reuse changes."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "No managed instrumentation capability gate changed. A concrete backend still must accept options using the original quote, bind the actual source/session/origin, observe equations in that same context, collect via the original native scope and deliver protected records through shared ordinary/controlled drivers.",
    "Cumulative host math proves ordinary schedule destination storage only, not native equation workspace, actual tensor provenance, capture invocation quotas or completion. It rejects independent invocation plans in this selected mechanism.",
    "Source publication counts retained payload rather than discovery/admission construction peaks. Successful borrowed revalidation is allocation-free by source review; later preflight vectors and copied checkpoints remain separate preparation obligations.",
    "Default options admission rejects every supplied source, even an empty plan with nonzero physical payload. Source sharing on an existing detached host fork does not grant native snapshot/fork or resumed capture support.",
    "No new released-checkpoint comparison, process-memory measurement or native distributed validation. Full observation, intervention, speculative, media and distributed integration remains unfinished."
  ]
}
